Description: Expand wildcard file arguments when archiving
 BBS software such as Mystic packs QWK and other packets with
 lha -a -i archive "dir/*": the quoted pattern is not expanded by the shell,
 and cmd.exe never expands wildcards on Windows, so lha found no file and
 created no archive. When archiving, an argument that names no existing file
 but contains * or ? is now expanded by lha (glob on Unix, _findfirst on
 Windows). Existing files, including names that contain those characters,
 and patterns without a match behave as before.
Author: Disconnected by Peer AT
Forwarded: no

